_spread":false,"_score_spread":0.0,"_gate_roic_consistency":1.9091818392987518,"_gp_roic_consistency":false,"_score_roic_consistency":0.0,"_gate_incr_roic":0.4486364780992164,"_gp_incr_roic":true,"_score_incr_roic":100.0,"_gate_margin_advantage":1.7063219563684697,"_gp_margin_advantage":true,"_score_margin_advantage":100.0,"_gate_pool_share":1.0,"_gp_pool_share":true,"_score_pool_share":100.0,"_gate_rev_durability":null,"_gp_rev_durability":null,"_score_rev_durability":0.0,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":0.0,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":0.0,"_gate_fund_growth":0,"_gp_fund_growth":false,"_score_fund_growth":0.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.0,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":false,"_score_shrhldr_yield":11.1,"_gate_share_shrink":null,"_gp_share_shrink":null,"_score_share_shrink":0.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.06917833121250681,"_gp_sbc_dilution":false,"_score_sbc_dilution":0.0,"_gate_insider_own":0.17984,"_gp_insider_own":true,"_score_insider_own":100.0,"_gate_insider_buying":null,"_gp_insider_buying":null,"_score_insider_buying":null,"pf":[],"description_full":"Five Point Holdings, LLC designs, develops, and owns mixed-use planned communities in California, the United States. It operates through Valencia, San Francisco, Great Park, and Hearthstone segments. The company sells residential and commercial land sites to homebuilders, commercial developers, and commercial buyers. It also provides development management services; and asset management services to land banking funds that are primarily focused on acquiring, developing, and managing residential lot option programs. The company was formerly known as Newhall Holding Company, LLC and changed its name to Five Point Holdings, LLC in May 2016. Five Point Holdings, LLC was incorporated in 2009 and is headquartered in Irvine, California.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Daniel C. Hedigan J.D. | President & CEO | Age 71 | Compensation: $3.5M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 90 people. Revenue per employee of $1.2M ranks in the below the sector median among Real Estate peers, with revenue growing 12%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $1.2M of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $85K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 3\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity).","financial_summary":["Five Point Holdings, LLC is a small-cap real estate business with a $690M market cap on $110M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +37% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder. Operating margins are expanding by +44.7pp year-over-year, which is one of the strongest signals that the moat is deepening.","Returns on capital run at 6% against a 9% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The business throws off $105M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 95 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.48\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and interest coverage of 40\u00d7 is fortress-like.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 18% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is, and within its sector the business captures 9.8\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Piotroski score 3/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.8) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Carries a 2088% premium to sector median EV/EBITDA","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":20.876906955958948},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Financial quality metrics lag Real Estate peers","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Interest-rate sensitivity and tenant-credit risk \u2014 cap rates and refinancing costs move faster than the 10-year leases can absorb.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Remote work structural vacancy \u2014 the post-pandemic shift to hybrid work has permanently impaired demand for urban office space across most markets.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Climate and insurance cost escalation \u2014 rising premiums and coverage withdrawals in flood/fire zones are repricing assets that the market once treated as perpetuities.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Operating margins 171% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","Trading at a 76% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Growing faster than most Real Estate peers \u2014 taking share inside the profit pool","Among the least levered in Real Estate \u2014 the fortress balance sheet in its peer set","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk","Real Estate sector showing strong relative momentum, outperforming the market by 6% over 3 months"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Fisher & Paykel Healthcare (ASX:FPH): Why Did the Medtech Reach a Record This Week?","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/au/stocks/healthcare/fisher-paykel-healthcare-asxfph-why-did-the-medtech-reach-a-record-this-week","date":"2026-11-27","timestamp":1795755840.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.026,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[